                <pb facs="0962" n="864" xml:id="pg864"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Tower.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-02-12"><hi rendition="#italic">February 12,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 124.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 152, of November 18; No. 157, of November 25, and your No. 165, of December
                    9 last, relative to the modification of the protocol for the arbitration of the
                    United States claims growing out of the Russian seizures of American sealing and
                    whaling vessels.</p>
                <p>The Department awaits the result of its telegraphic instruction of December 5
                    last relative thereto.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
